      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "osSgs",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 20,
          "name": "spec_title",
          "fill": "$text-hi",
          "content": "Spec — pi runtime (539) · v1",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "U9ync",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "spec_sub",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 1452,
          "content": "pi (`pi` 0.85.1, npm @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent) becomes the fifth agent runtime. Almost all of it reuses shipped surfaces — the Agents row, the runtime pickers, the Skills pane — so the new pixels are the provider mark from #593 and the words on existing controls; the permission control disappears for pi rather than gaining words. This frame shows the mark beside the four shipped marks, the rail before and after, the Agents row, trust and permissions (decision 6, signed off 2026-09-18), and the tint (decision 11, option 1, decided 2026-09-18). Probe evidence, the code inventory and decisions 1–11 are in docs/features/539-pi-runtime.md.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Q6x4sG",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 100,
          "name": "cap_a",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "A · THE MARK — pi.dev's PIXEL-π, THREE BLOCKS; RUNNER PAINTS ONE MASK IN ONE TINT, SO IT IS DRAWN THREE WAYS",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
