          "x": 944,
          "y": 671,
          "name": "D · trust and permissions",
          "width": 532,
          "fill": "$panel",
          "cornerRadius": 8,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 12,
          "padding": 14,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "wV74l",
              "name": "Chats",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "zuKvw",
                  "name": "hdr",
                  "gap": 8,
                  "alignItems": "center",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "tbBkJ",
                      "name": "n",
                      "fill": "$text-hi",
                      "content": "Chats",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Wjqpm",
                      "name": "f",
                      "fill": "$text-low",
                      "content": "no flag",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "DdUHa",
                  "name": "d",
                  "fill": "$text-mid",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The role form and slot overrides hide the permission control; the app-wide mission permission mode leaves pi argv untouched. In a folder with .agents/skills or .pi resources, pi opens its own “Trust project folder?” dialog before the session starts. A human is at the prompt, answers it, and pi saves the answer as usual.",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 10,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "rPd0i",
              "name": "Mission slots",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 3,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "Xgu0i",
                  "name": "hdr",
                  "gap": 8,
                  "alignItems": "center",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "L6hsX",
                      "name": "n",
                      "fill": "$text-hi",
                      "content": "Mission slots",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 12,
                      "fontWeight": "500"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "UafHi",
                      "name": "f",
                      "fill": "$text-low",
                      "content": "--approve",
                      "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "MEq2j",
                  "name": "d",
                  "fill": "$text-mid",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "An unattended slot would sit on that dialog with no status signal (it emits no ui_prompt event). --approve is pi's one-run trust override: the folder is trusted for that run and nothing is written to ~/.pi/agent/trust.json. Cost accepted: the project's own .pi extensions and settings load, the same boundary the crew's bash tool already has, since pi has no sandbox. This is what the app-wide Bypass default for mission slots (#527) means for pi.",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                  "fontSize": 10,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
