                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "c3eGt",
                      "name": "n",
                      "fill": "$text-low",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "Not taken. Faithful to pi.dev, but it needs a new render path: a layered ChatIcon variant painting three masks in one slot, with the stopped rule (#641) dimming all three to one grey. It would be the only multi-hue mark in a rail built on one hue per provider, and at 12 px each block is 6 px.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.45,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
                      "fontSize": 10,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Ls7lS",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1339,
          "name": "cap_rule",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "RULES",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "TpH6o",
          "x": 24,
          "y": 1361,
          "name": "notes_rule",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "The mark is identity, never state (#593), and stopped marks lose their hue (#641): whichever tint is chosen, a stopped pi row draws the silhouette in $text-1 at 0.45, so the three options differ only while a session runs.\n\nA wrong logo is worse than a generic one. Until the runtime enum knows `pi`, a pi session is an unknown runtime and draws the speech bubble; the mark appears only once the session's stored runtime is `pi`.\n\nThe silhouette is pi's own: pi.dev's favicon is this shape in one colour, so the mono options are not a Runner invention. The geometry is a 4 × 4 grid of 6-unit cells in the 24-unit box, so it lands on whole pixels at 12 and 24 px.\n\nThe Agents row, the runtime pickers and the Skills pane are the shipped components with new words. pi has no permission modes, so the role form and slot overrides hide that control instead of listing modes. Nothing on this frame is a new control.\n\nWindows draws the same mark from the same bundled bytes; the tint is applied at paint time.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "PyUYP",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 1339,
          "name": "cap_code",
          "fill": "$text-low",
          "content": "IMPLEMENTATION",
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "u9Gez",
          "x": 756,
          "y": 1361,
          "name": "notes_code",
          "fill": "$text-mid",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 700,
          "content": "assets.rs: `PI` traced from pi.dev/logo.svg (three axis-aligned rectangles on a 117.36-unit grid), written as one path in `viewBox -2 -2 28 28` with the eye as a reverse-wound subpath: `M0 0h18v12h-6v6H6v6H0zM6 6v6h6V6zM18 12h6v12h-6z`. One `ASSETS` row, `pi.svg`; the licence block gains pi's line (MIT, earendil-works).\n\nchat_icon.rs: `Some(Runtime::Pi) => (\"pi.svg\", theme::text())`, the Codex treatment. No colour constant, no layered variant; the three-colour component on this file is the record of option 3, not an asset.\n\nTests: `pane_identity_icon`, `sidebar_tab_icon`, `command_palette.rs`, `settings/archived.rs`, the `assets.rs` registration test and the `chat_icon.rs` tint table each gain a `pi` row.\n\nThe D copy is the spec's decision 6 as signed off. `runners/logic.rs::permission_modes` returns `&[]` for pi, which hides the control; `--approve` is added beside `mission_bus_sandbox_args` in spawn.rs for mission slots only.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-ui",
          "fontSize": 10,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
